<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         THE INSPECTOR'S CHROME GRAMMAR, ON THE FIRE LAYER (0.50).

         The FOURTH converted grammar file, after `Views/Dialogs/DialogStyles`,
         `Views/Settings/SettingsStyles` and `Views/Shell/ShellChromeStyles`.
         Same mechanism, and the reason it is the right one: this file is
         included by exactly four views — `InspectorView` (which hosts all
         eight tabs, so the classes cascade to every one of them regardless of
         its own DataContext), `MixerInspectorView`, `PhraseCatalogView` and
         `StemMixerView` — so re-pointing it moves ~76 KB of tab markup at once.
         Editing eight views by hand would have converted eight things that
         then drift apart.

         WHAT CHANGED AND WHAT DID NOT: every class NAME survives, and several
         are load-bearing (`InspectorCard` is asserted by name in
         `Perf/InspectorConstructionUiPerfSmokeTests`, `Disclosure` +
         `DisclosureLabel` by `UI/InspectorDisclosureWiringTests`). Every SHAPE
         moved: radius 4/6/10 became the Fire 4/6/10 ladder, the opaque
         `#181A1E`/`#131519` surfaces became washes of white over the pane, the
         app's `#24272B` border became the layer's ONE hairline, and the
         section labels became the layer's signature mark — a MONO EYEBROW
         (9.5 px, .24em, dim) over the card it opens.

         ─── THE LADDER RULE ──────────────────────────────────────────────
         Only `FireRadius*` / `FireSize*` / `FirePad*` / `FireGap*` /
         `FireSpace*` may appear below. Several app steps do not exist on the
         Fire ladders, so one stray `RadiusSm` is a corner 2 px rounder than
         its neighbours — invisible in a diff. Pinned by the default-gate
         `UI/FireStyleClassTests.EachConvertedGrammar_ReachesOnlyForFireLadderTokens`
         (plus the companion proving the file really SPEAKS the layer, so "no
         app tokens because no tokens at all" cannot pass).

         TWO app keys survive on purpose and are NOT ladder steps:
         `FieldLabelRail` (84) and `RowHeightField` (32) are this pane's own
         geometry. The Fire ladder's nearest row height is `FireFieldHeight`
         = 36, which is a full-width settings row — the inspector is a ~380 px
         dock pane where density IS the design, and four extra pixels per row
         costs a whole field over a card.

         ─── NO `Transitions` SETTER, EVER ────────────────────────────────
         Every one of the eight tabs is `IsVisible`-gated and a hidden
         control's style clocks keep ticking (DotCharter.UI/AGENTS.md), and it
         is also the Fire layer's own rule — hover is instant on every other
         converted surface. The two that used to be here (the M/S buttons and
         the technique chip) are gone. Pinned by
         `UI/FireStyleClassTests.TheInspectorGrammar_CarriesNoTransitionsSetter`.

         A `Cursor` setter IS allowed here, unlike in the other three grammars:
         nothing constructs an inspector view without an Avalonia platform
         (`SettingsSearchTests` is the reason that ban exists and it does not
         reach these views), and 42 `Button.Subtle` actions losing the hand
         cursor would be a real regression. The same test states that in
         reverse so the difference is deliberate rather than forgotten.
         ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

    <Styles.Resources>
        <ResourceDictionary>
            <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
                <!-- A DROPDOWN'S CHROME IS A RESOURCE KEY, NEVER A STYLE
                     SELECTOR. Avalonia's ComboBox template sets its popup
                     Border's Background / BorderBrush / BorderThickness /
                     CornerRadius / Padding from a `{DynamicResource …}` written
                     INSIDE the template — a LOCAL value, which beats any style
                     setter. `Styles/FireMenuChrome.axaml` restates those keys in
                     Fire values, and merging it HERE scopes it: a resource
                     lookup from inside a popup walks up to the control that
                     opened it, i.e. to this grammar. Without it the inspector's
                     ~26 pickers keep opening in Fluent's #1c1d28 at radius 5
                     while everything around them is on the layer. Read that
                     file's own header before touching a popup, and see
                     `UI/EditorChromeTests`, which pins every literal in it
                     against the Fire token it restates. -->
                <ResourceInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/FireMenuChrome.axaml" />
            </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        </ResourceDictionary>
    </Styles.Resources>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         THE GRAMMAR ITSELF, BY SECTION. Every `<Style>` this file used to
         declare inline now lives in `Views/Editor/InspectorStyles/`, sliced
         along the section banners it already carried and moved byte for byte.

         ORDER IS THE CONTRACT. Avalonia applies styles in the order it walks
         this collection and a later selector wins, so these includes stand in
         the exact order the sections stood in the one file. It matters more
         here than in most grammars: this file RESTATES app classes
         (`Button.Subtle`, `ToggleButton.Seg`, …) that are also declared
         app-wide, and a restatement only wins because it is applied later.

         The `Styles.Resources` block above stays in this file. Merging
         `FireMenuChrome.axaml` HERE is what SCOPES it — a resource lookup
         from inside a popup walks up to the control that opened it, i.e. to
         this grammar — and pushing it down into a part would change the node
         that walk arrives at.
         ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter/Views/Editor/InspectorStyles/PickersAndAppClasses.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter/Views/Editor/InspectorStyles/TabStripAndMixerRow.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter/Views/Editor/InspectorStyles/PaneChromeAndTechniqueChip.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter/Views/Editor/InspectorStyles/ScopeAndIssueChrome.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter/Views/Editor/InspectorStyles/EqModule.axaml" />

</Styles>
